# r9 -- SELinux COMPILED IN, OFF FOR taOS. Built 2026-10-30 on omarchy.
#
# Why: Luma (a kexec guest) ships SELINUX=enforcing and its rpm-ostree/podman
# stack expects labels. One shared kernel, per-boot choice
# (~/.taos-team/SELINUX-luma-research-20261030.md, recommendation 2).
#
# How taOS stays off: `selinux` is REMOVED from the CONFIG_LSM default order,
# so the taOS boot (whose cmdline carries no lsm=) initialises exactly the
# LSMs it did on r8. Only kexec-guest.sh --guest luma names selinux in lsm=.
# This deliberately fails pmOS's kconfig "hardening" check, which wants
# selinux in CONFIG_LSM; the alternative is a taOS cmdline change in the
# boot image, a second thing to carry.
#
# SECURITY_SELINUX_DEVELOP=y is what makes `enforcing=0` on the guest cmdline
# work, so an unlabelled Luma root can boot permissive for its first relabel.
# SECURITY_NETWORK and AUDIT are dependencies of SECURITY_SELINUX: without
# them the symbol is hidden, not merely unset, and a hand-added line is dropped.
#
# Waydroid: NO change needed. ANDROID_BINDER_IPC=y with the static
# binder,hwbinder,vndbinder devices was already on, and pmOS's kconfig
# "waydroid" check REQUIRES ANDROID_BINDERFS to stay unset.
#
# Resolved with `make olddefconfig` in the pmbootstrap native chroot;
# `make listnewconfig` printed nothing, so the build cannot stop on a prompt.
# The VERSION/CC_* hunks are the edge toolchain (clang 22.1.8 -> 23.1.4),
# recomputed by every build, not choices.
#
# Needs `pkgrel=9` AND `pmbootstrap build --force`: the binary repo carries
# 7.2.9-r2, so without --force pmbootstrap reports the local 7.2.2-r9 "up to
# date" and exits 0 having built nothing.
